From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local.invalid>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 01:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] enhancement_pair: wait for late Dolby Vision EL frames

The enhancement pair queue previously treated a full base-layer queue as
evidence that no matching enhancement frame would arrive. After an arbitrary
MPEG-TS seek the BL decoder can fill all 16 slots before the EL decoder emits
its first recovered picture, causing the first paired frame to be rendered
without FEL depending on decoder scheduling.

Keep the bounded BL queue as backpressure, but only give up when the EL reaches
EOF or has advanced past the BL PTS. This prevents the scheduling race without
growing the queue or changing single-layer playback.
---
 filters/f_enhancement_pair.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/filters/f_enhancement_pair.c b/filters/f_enhancement_pair.c
index 18cea54..4acae51 100644
--- a/filters/f_enhancement_pair.c
+++ b/filters/f_enhancement_pair.c
@@ -159,8 +159,7 @@ static void pair_process(struct mp_filter *f)
         // No EL match for the oldest BL. Hold BL unless we have affirmative
         // evidence no EL is coming.
         bool give_up = p->el_eof ||
-                       (p->num_el_pending > 0 && cmp > 0) ||
-                       p->num_bl_pending >= QUEUE_MAX;
+                       (p->num_el_pending > 0 && cmp > 0);
         if (!give_up)
             return;
 
